  "explanation": "Python evaluates a default argument value exactly once, when the function is defined — not once per call. So every call to add_item that omits `basket` shares the exact same list object. checkout(['apple', 'bread']) appends into that shared list, and the very next call checkout(['milk']) keeps appending into the same list rather than starting fresh, so `second` comes back as ['apple', 'bread', 'milk'] instead of just ['milk'] — state leaks between two calls that look completely independent from the caller's point of view.",
